# What the image build does NOT need, and what it costs to send anyway.
#
# The build context is streamed to the daemon before anything runs, so an
# entry here is time saved on every build. The two big ones are deliberate:
# `mdb/` holds the realm databases (`test:realm` converts them; the image
# never does) and `captures/` holds 218 recorded sessions for the corpus
# replay. `resources/world/` is NOT excluded — the converted world is what
# ships, and the app reads it at runtime.

.git
.github
node_modules
dist
out
.scratch
todo

# Recorded sessions and the realm databases: build inputs for the test suite
# and the world conversion, never for the application.
captures
mdb
mega-paramud

# Prose. None of it is read by a build, and `docs/greatermud/` alone is large.
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Anything of the user's that might be sitting in a working tree. The image
# must never carry somebody's options file, and the extraResources filter in
# package.json says the same thing one layer further in.
resources/config/user.yaml*
resources/config/*.local.*
resources/config/profiles
resources/config/realms
resources/config/memory
resources/config/fights
resources/config/mob-lore.json*

# Build artefacts and editor droppings.
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
